WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.730
Obsessed with Smartphones.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.530
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.920
Is that fun?

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.790
It can be at times.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:51.540
Like when?

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.000
Like when I'm able to 
make something like this.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.470
It's a polar bear.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.570
Hey, how'd you make it?

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.510
It's a secret.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.640
You're quite talented.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.100
Can I take a picture?

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.090
A picture? You have a camera?

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.950
Not a camera, exactly.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.190
I bought a sumafo (smartphone).

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.900
What's a sumafo?

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.320
That would be you rolled 
up in a reed mat <i>(sumaki)</i>.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.320
Those are rice dumplings wrapped 
in bamboo leaves <i>(chimaki)</i>.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.580
Certain Victory

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:23.580
Headband <i>(hachimaki)</i>.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.090
Cigars <i>(hamaki)</i>.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.390
Yellowtail <i>(hamachi)</i>!

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.440
Kimchi <i>(kimuchi)</i>!

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.460
I said sumafo! As in smartphone!

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.840
A sumafo, it's a kind of cell phone.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.930
Oh, Mr. Penguin, is that 
one of those sumafos?

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.000
I don't know much about them either.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.460
You neither?

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.980
What can it do?

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.620
It's really convenient.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:50.890
There are lots of apps too.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.520
And you can look up maps and such.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.530
You can browse the Internet too! See?

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.880
Aren't the words rather 
small and hard to read?

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.450
Not at all!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.650
That's when you do this.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.330
It's called punch control.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:08.820
You hit it?

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.240
No!

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.110
Don't you mean pinch control?

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:13.600
Same thing.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.530
I see.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:15.680
It is!

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.590
Now watch this, Miss Sasako.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.710
Are you sure it's actually convenient?

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.330
It's convenient, really!

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.520
Let's see, it goes like this...

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.520
It'll get easier to use over time.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.940
Oh, you have one, too, Polar Bear?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.690
Yup. Here, check it out.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:38.670
You go like this.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.570
Wow, that's so cool!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.450
You're so talented, Mr. Polar Bear!

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:46.450
It's nothing, really.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.370
I folded an iris.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.030
That's amazing!

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.190
You really are talented!

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.500
All right! Look at this!

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.160
You go like this...

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.040
Take that!

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.010
And that!

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.920
It's no use.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.250
Don't worry. You just 
have to get used to it.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.220
Somehow, you sound condescending.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.720
I have a sumafo, as well.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.480
Oh, really?

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.370
Yes.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.660
I hear what you're saying,

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.590
but are you sure you can
 actually use it, Mr. Llama?

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.690
Of course.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.560
Just watch.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.540
Wow, that's amazing! 
Such flexible technique!

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:31.720
I see now!

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.550
Oh, do you want to exchange profiles?

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:37.690
For sure!

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.300
I know some really cool apps.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.550
Ooh, like what? Tell me!

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.740
Panda

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.150
We're totally in the 
sumafo generation!

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:52.480
Are we?

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:53.520
We are!

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:57.450
It's really convenient to 
have a sumafo!

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:58.650
In what way?

00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.980
Let's see...

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:04.410
You can control the screen by poking it.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:07.200
You can lick it.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.390
You can poke it with your beak.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:18.880
And the words are really 
tiny and hard to read!

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.930
Are you sure it's actually convenient?

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:23.690
Huh?

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:27.350
Anyway, a working panda like myself

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:29.580
cannot possibly get by

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.470
without a cell phone.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.820
You'll get by just fine.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:34.810
You don't need one.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.650
I don't like that train of thought.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.520
What about it?

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.260
You see, if something happens,

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.030
it'd be really convenient 
to have a cell phone.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:46.240
If something happens, huh?

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:52.020
Hey, we're out of balsamic vinegar.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:55.490
Could you get some on 
your way home from work?

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:58.210
Sure thing.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.700
It <i>is</i> convenient!

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.310
All right, I'll buy you one.

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:05.790
Hooray!

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:09.570
Here, look!

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:10.720
What is it?

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.730
I made the picture I took the other day

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.430
my standby screen wallpaper.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.290
Are you not making anything 
with origami today?

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:19.570
If I feel like it.

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:21.040
You're more impressed with that?!

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:22.440
Hello!

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:24.860
Welcome!

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.070
You seem really happy, Panda.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.320
Well, you see...

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.660
Oh, that's...

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.700
It's a sumafo with a panda cover!

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.000
It's very cute!

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.280
It is, isn't it?

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:41.460
It was really hard to find.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.180
How's the sumafo?

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.880
It's very convenient.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:51.270
See? You can check the 
weather forecast whenever you want.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:59.580
And you can look up maps 
so you don't get lost.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.360
You can put it on your head

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:07.530
and improve your balance, too!

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:10.620
That's not proper 
sumafo usage, though.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.530
He seems to be using it

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.050
better than you though, Mr. Penguin.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:17.830
B-But I changed my standby screen!

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.910
Also...

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.750
I can take pictures!

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.380
And I can listen to music!

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.920
I-It's okay, Panda!

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.290
Looks like the only thing 
that broke was the cover.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.230
So it seems.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.000
So cheer up!

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.040
It's a good thing the sumafo is safe.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:52.920
Here you go, Panda.

00:07:56.980 --> 00:07:58.790
But for me,

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:03.040
the sumafo was an accessory 
to the panda cover.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.130
Oh.

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:17.270
Hey, where's your sumaho?

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:18.600
I just called you.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:21.810
Hey, can you hear me?

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:25.010
Bal-sa-mic vin-e-gar, got it?

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:28.270
Bal-sam-ic vin-e-gar!

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:33.210
We're sorry, your call cannot 
be completed at this time.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:39.740
Sumahos aren't convenient 
at all, are they?

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:43.260
You know, it's called a "smartphone,"

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:46.080
so it's "sumafo," not "sumaho."

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.880
Why does it matter?

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.380
Hello!

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:56.550
Could I get my usual, Polar Bear?

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.600
Are you feeling better, Panda?

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:01.310
What do you mean?

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.980
Apparently I was an idiot for worrying.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.970
Your sumafo is right here, Panda.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.230
Oh.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.920
I don't need the sumafo anymore.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:12.990
Are you just trying to act tough?

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:14.720
No, I'm serious.

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:17.250
It's not even a panda.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:21.330
What?  You just bought it, 
you should use it.

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:26.260
Look, Panda. A sumafo case.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:28.750
I tried folding something like this.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.340
Oh! It's a panda!

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.760
This time, it's made out 
of paper so it won't break.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.160
Good for you.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.970
You're amazing, Mr. Polar Bear!

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.930
Pandas <i>are</i> awesome!

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:07.960
Polar
Bear's
Café

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:12.920
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:12.480
Super Fun Driving Lesson

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.500
What's wrong, Mr. Penguin?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:20.590
Did you get food poisoning?

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:22.690
No, nothing like that!

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:24.560
It's about Miss Penko, isn't it?

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.450
N-No, it's not!

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:28.770
I'm going to a driver's training school.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.770
He's trying to get his driver's license.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.420
Why all of a sudden?

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:36.240
He wants to ask Miss 
Penko out for a drive.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.450
H-How do you know that?!

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.910
You wrote about it on your blog.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.450
Oh, Miss Penko, Miss Penko,

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.960
I want to take you on 
a drive by the ocean.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:51.580
Thus I am going to driving school.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.290
Don't read people's diaries 
without permission!

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:57.500
Well, blogs are meant for others to read.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:58.980
If you don't want others to read it,

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:00.870
you should make your blog private.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.260
Your blog is now private.

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.930
Is driving school hard?

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.910
It's pretty hard.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:12.070
Is driving a car that hard?

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.220
Yeah.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:16.090
The instructor is really mean

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:19.110
and I wasn't able to parallel park today.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:22.160
Parallel parking is always hard at first.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:23.900
It is.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:26.120
Parallel parking <i>(jyuretsu chusha)</i>?

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.230
Ten cars in a row <i>(jyuretsu chusha)</i>?

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:35.240
Ten shots in a row <i>(jyuretsu chusha)</i>?

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:41.160
Ten headbands in a row <i>(jyuretsu kachusha)</i>?

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:47.050
Ten kisses in a row <i>(jyuretsu chuu)</i>?

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:55.110
So we're meeting at 11 tomorrow.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:58.840
Jeez, weren't you listening at all?

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:00.720
We're going to go study.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.290
We are?

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:04.770
Mr. Polar Bear is going to

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:07.090
show Mr. Penguin the techniques of driving.

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:09.240
You don't have anything better 
to do anyways, do you, Panda?

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.500
I'll be too busy relaxing.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.330
That would mean you have time.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.560
Oh, whatever.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.940
Then do you not want to come driving?

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.080
Oh, we're going on a drive?

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:22.300
Of course I'll come!

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:25.960
Jeez. Then we'll meet tomorrow 
right outside the café.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:26.940
Okay!

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.270
I wonder what's taking Panda so long.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.690
Should we go get him?

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.090
He'll be here soon enough.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:39.070
Good morning.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.150
You're late, Panda.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:44.280
What's with the bamboo?!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:47.490
You always need snacks 
when you go for a drive.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:50.530
I brought enough for everyone!

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.480
Um, I don't need any.

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:54.960
Not to mention that snack 
is only for you, Panda.

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:56.600
Snacks <i>(oyatsu)</i>?

00:12:58.150 --> 00:12:59.590
That's a heated table <i>(kotatsu)</i>.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.380
That's a step ladder <i>(kyatatsu)</i>.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.130
That's a cabbage <i>(kyabetsu)</i>.

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.240
Come on, let's get going already.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.930
Where's Mr. Llama?

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.130
He had to work at the zoo today.

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.510
All right, let's get 
going then, Polar Bear.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.690
The backseats in cars 
are always questionable.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.140
They're never big enough 
to sleep comfortably on.

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:24.530
Sit up straight back there, Panda.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:25.900
Okay, here we go.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:37.180
Amazing. You handled 
starting the car like a pro.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:38.320
It's nothing, really.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.500
So what's the secret?

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.710
Well, let's see...

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.450
Once you feel like this,

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:44.930
you do this,

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.210
and go!

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:48.090
That's it.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.330
That's a little too abstract.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:51.940
I don't understand any of it.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:53.830
Mr. Penguin.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:54.560
What?

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.960
It's probably something 
like when you're

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:59.170
swinging from a tire swing.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:00.980
You're making it 
even more confusing!

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.360
So, where are we going?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.460
How about the mountains?

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:07.930
Especially one where there's 
plenty of bamboo grass.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.560
Somewhere around here is just fine.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.090
The whole point of this trip is so

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:17.080
I can learn Polar Bear's 
driving techniques.

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:30.610
When did you get your 
license, Polar Bear?

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:32.180
When I became an adult.

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:35.140
Congratulations 
on New Store Opening

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:35.140
That's not exactly what I meant...

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.120
It's finished.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.890
Thank you very much!

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.560
<i>Bamboo grass?</i>

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:48.830
Hello there, Panda.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:52.030
Are you going on a trip?

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:53.410
I'm having a snack!

00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:58.250
Bye-bye!

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:05.130
Aw, I'm really hungry.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.980
You were just eating bamboo grass!

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:09.970
Let's go there!

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:12.430
Drive-thru

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.480
Welcome, are you ready to order?

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.190
Could I get bamboo or 
bamboo grass, please?

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:29.400
I'm terribly sorry, 
that is not on our menu.

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:32.320
We'll come back.

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:47.630
Welcome, are you ready to order?

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:49.210
Can I get a fish burger?

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.050
But I want the fish raw!

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:54.600
I'm terribly sorry, 
that is not on our menu.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:57.390
We'll come back.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.730
Welcome, are you ready to order?

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:10.290
I couldn't think of a good joke,

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:11.200
so I'll come back.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.240
Um, I beg your pardon.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:16.560
Welcome—

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.580
That's why I'm telling you 
to get the fish burger meal!

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.720
The lettuce burger meal is better.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.100
It's not bamboo grass, but it is a leaf.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:26.040
The teriyaki burger meal is better.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.840
All right.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.590
Then...

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.270
Are you ready?

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:33.510
We'll come back!

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:36.770
Um, you don't need to 
drive in circles!

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:38.720
You can stay there until you decide!

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:42.260
Thank you for your order.

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:45.200
Please go to the next 
window to pick it up.

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:46.740
Okay.

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:55.790
Is this it?

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:58.590
Please don't play in the drive-thru!

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:01.940
What do you think, Mr. Penguin?

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:03.940
Did you think you get the technique down?

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:05.720
For what?

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:08.360
The technique for playing 
in a drive-thru?

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:12.460
I would like to learn the 
techniques of driving.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:16.490
Hey, Polar Bear, aren't you 
going to do that thing?

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:17.430
That thing?

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:20.460
You know, Lord Straw 
Stalk <i>(Warashibe Chouja)</i>.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:22.340
You mean parallel parking 
<i>(jyuretsu chusha)</i>?

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:23.680
Yeah, that!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.470
Those are two completely 
different things.

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:27.770
Good job on figuring that 
out, Mr. Penguin.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:31.290
Come on, Polar Bear, you should try it!

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:33.780
Show me a driving technique!

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:36.200
Okay.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.700
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:42.410
Okay, let's do it here.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:44.500
Make sure you watch carefully.

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:47.920
Look carefully at your 
surroundings, and then back up.

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:49.960
So look carefully and then back up.

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:52.000
The trick is...

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:53.690
The trick?

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.500
...it's really easy to see

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.520
when you stick your head out up here.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.930
I can't do that, though!

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:00.650
Jeez.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:03.390
What is it?

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.350
Is everything okay? 
Did you hit something?

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.480
Hey, Miss Sasako!

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:11.820
Oh, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:14.320
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:17.240
Are you all going for a drive today?

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.280
Where are you all headed?

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:20.780
It is an aimless journey.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:22.990
Where are you headed, Miss Sasako?

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:25.400
I'm just heading home.

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:27.450
Oh, I know.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.760
Here, I'll share these with you.

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:31.920
Bagels?

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:35.280
I heard that a really 
good place opened up,

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:36.740
so I went to get some.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:41.890
Thank you! I was just getting hungry.

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:47.250
You just keep eating.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:49.710
I'm a growing panda.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:18:59.030
Oh, I'm fine.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:01.820
There's always room for bamboo grass.

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:09.580
It looks like Panda's still 
eating, even in his dreams.

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:14.160
Mr. Penguin?

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.270
I-I'm not asleep!

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:20.760
I-I would never be so rude as to 
fall asleep in the passenger seat!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.300
If you don't speak up,

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:25.720
I can't tell if you asleep or awake, Mr. Penguin.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:28.640
I'm awake! Seriously! Trust me!

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:31.870
Well, I wouldn't care if you were asleep.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.900
Don't make me sound like Panda!

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:37.110
I'm going to learn the 
techniques of driving!

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:40.320
Are you going to buy a car 
once you get your license?

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:44.740
I'm not sure.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:48.540
Mini-vans like this are good, too.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:54.270
Those are really cool, too.

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:03.090
There's something I want 
to show you, Miss Penko.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.720
Oh, I wonder what it could be?

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:05.930
Look,

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:08.320
over there.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:13.400
What's that?

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.360
They're flying fish.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.530
Oh, my.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.990
It's all you can eat.

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:26.950
How wonderful.

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:40.950
Miss Penko...

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.000
Bamboo grass everywhere.

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:55.920
A bagel <i>(be-guru)</i>.

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.310
An eagle <i>(iiguru)</i>.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:01.850
A saber <i>(sa-beru)</i>.

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:06.410
Yodel <i>(yo-deru)</i>.

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:12.970
It's a little lonely when 
there's no one to retort.

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:20.630
W-What's going on?!

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:25.130
This would be...

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:26.550
It would be... <i>(panku)</i>

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:28.970
That would be a dunk <i>(danku)</i>.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:32.070
That would be ink <i>(inku)</i>.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:34.500
That would be pink <i>(pinku)</i>.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:37.020
That would be a skunk <i>(sukanku)</i>.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:39.260
That was great.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:41.170
What are you talking about?

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:42.230
That's not good at all.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:45.480
What are we going to do, Mr. Penguin?

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:47.040
I'm not sure.

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:49.450
Maybe we should call a car dealership?

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:52.110
No need to panic.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:53.660
In times like this...

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:57.910
I can just pull it back home.

00:21:57.910 --> 00:21:59.530
I see.

00:21:59.530 --> 00:22:02.340
The trick is to wrap your 
nails around the bumper.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:06.350
It's a good thing he's 
teaching you all this.

00:22:06.350 --> 00:22:09.050
I'm definitely not going 
to be able to repeat this.

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:11.920
Well, you know...

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:14.480
This is amusing, so I'm going 
to take a picture anyway.

00:22:17.460 --> 00:22:24.860
Polar
 Bear's
  Café

00:23:54.930 --> 00:24:24.440
Next Time

00:23:57.890 --> 00:24:02.080
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin, 
tell me a funny story.

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:03.310
Jeez, Panda.

00:24:03.310 --> 00:24:05.400
That's a textbook way 
to put me on the spot.

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:10.050
Then can I think of you as 
my loyal servant as of today?

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:10.800
No.

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:14.240
Mr. Penguin, you're the 
textbook definition of stingy.

00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:15.410
Polar Bear.

00:24:15.410 --> 00:24:18.450
Well then, next week 
on Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:19.590
Rock, paper—

00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:21.760
Hey! Would you cut that out?

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:24.440
Panda gets Enthusiastic
Everyone's Parfait

00:24:21.760 --> 00:24:23.150
Enjoy!
